Build the SDK for Windows x64 with llvm-mingw (Clang, libc++, MinGW-w64 UCRT) as well as clang-cl (kuf-cod-recomp M16)

- Windows headers by their lower-case names (windows.h, winsock2.h, ws2tcpip.h, objbase.h, sdkddkver.h): the names
  MinGW-w64 installs, which MSVC's case-insensitive lookup accepts too; needed when cross-building on Linux.
- rex/chrono: the clock_time_conversion / clock_cast fallback for every libc++, not only Apple's.
- FFmpeg under MinGW: an overlay config.h takes config_windows_x86_64.h and sets HAVE_LIBC_MSVCRT to 0, as FFmpeg's
  own configure does for MinGW (the MSVC branch includes crtversion.h). FFmpeg itself is unchanged.
- XInput: GetProcAddress results stored with reinterpret_cast (Clang rejects the implicit function-to-void* cast).
- Thread names: the debugger exception needs MSVC's __try; under MinGW SetThreadDescription alone names the thread.
- Guest imports (__imp__Name) exported from the runtime DLL explicitly under MinGW (REX_FUNC_EXPORT in rex/hook.h):
  the MinGW linker's automatic export skips every __imp_* name. The project links rexruntime with
  --export-all-symbols so the rest stays exported.
- Cross builds: the generated rexglue.cmake runs REXGLUE_HOST_REXGLUE (the build machine's code generator) instead
  of the target's rexglue program (which, on Linux with Wine registered for .exe files, would run under Wine).
  Only when the target system differs from the build machine (a Linux sysroot build runs its own).

